    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d344">

                <pb facs="0518" n="416" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg416"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 9160/68.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Chargé Sands.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1908-01-09"><hi rendition="#italic">January 9,
                        1908</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Root acknowledges Mr. Sand’s telegram of the 8th instant, and informs him
                    that the payment of $1,000 each to the two injured men and punishment of the
                    policemen who wounded them will be quite acceptable. Says the removal of
                    important officers of the Government is not asked, but that appropriate
                    reprimand to the commanding general may be in order. Mr. Root also states that
                    it is not desired to insist on the public humiliation of those officers, but
                    trusts to the good <pb facs="0519" n="417" xml:id="pg417"/> judgment of the
                    Guatemalan Government for appropriate disavowal of their acts, which it is
                    understood was practically offered and which will be greatly appreciated as
                    evidence of their friendly consideration.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
